questions.prompt:
A customer-service tool lets agents run operations on orders, such as *cancel order* and *partial refund*. These operations call external systems: the payment gateway and the warehouse. New requirements:

- every operation must appear in an audit log with a description;
- an agent can undo the last operation;
- failed operations should later be put on a queue and retried.

Which pattern best fits these requirements?

